      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "A roof in Utah typically lasts 15 to 30 years for standard asphalt shingles, though extreme UV rays, heavy snow, freeze-thaw cycles, and high-altitude weather often shorten the lifespan compared to milder climates.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "15 to 30 years"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Lifespan by Roof Material"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "3-Tab Asphalt Shingles: 15 to 20 years"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Architectural / Composition Shingles: 25 to 30+ years (or 20\u201325 years under heavy local stress)"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Metal Roofing: 40 to 70+ years"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Clay or Concrete Tile: 50 to 100 years",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              2,
              3
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Why Utah's Climate Affects Roof Lifespan"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Intense UV Radiation: High elevation means stronger ultraviolet rays, which dry out asphalt shingles, strip away protective granules, and make the material brittle.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Extreme Temperature Swings: Hot summer days followed by cold nights cause constant expansion and contraction, weakening shingle seals and leading to cracks.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              4
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Snow and Ice Dams: Heavy winter snow loads and ice dams trap moisture, putting extra stress on roof edges and underlayment.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Attic Ventilation: Poorly ventilated attics trap summer heat and cook shingles from the underside, accelerating wear.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Signs Your Utah Roof Is Reaching Its End"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Granule Loss: Finding small, pebble-like granules collecting heavily in your rain gutters or around the foundation."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Curling or Lifting Edges: Shingle corners warping or peeling upward from thermal stress and wind."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Age Milestone: Approaching or passing the 15 to 20-year mark for standard asphalt roofs."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Moss or Dark Streaks: Persistent moisture retention in shaded areas causing organic growth.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              4,
              5
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
